    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0554" n="458" xml:id="pg458"/>

                <head>No. 345.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-08-24"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 24, 1872</date>.
                        (Received September 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 617.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a copy of a note which I
                    have to-day addressed to the Mexican government, demanding, in pursuance of the
                    instructions contained in your No. 273, of the 1st instant, the prompt return of
                    Abraham Gonzales, kidnaped in Texas by one Pedro A. Valdes, and the punishment
                    of the perpetrator of that outrage.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d345-a1.xml" xpointer="d345-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
